        "original_id": "192ec327-2963-5265-a6c8-c95eee4f8378",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kathy Mattea, Don Williams, Richard Leigh\n- Products: “Come from the Heart”, Willow in the Wind, Traces, Old Friends\n- Topics: Don Williams discography, Kathy Mattea discography\n\nFacts:\n- Don Williams is an American country music artist, and this chunk references his detailed discography.\n- In 1987, Don Williams first recorded and released “Come from the Heart” on his album Traces.\n- In 1988, Richard Leigh, who was Clark’s husband, released “Come from the Heart” on his album Old Friends.\n- In 1989, Kathy Mattea released “Come from the Heart” as a single in conjunction with her album Willow in the Wind.\n- Kathy Mattea’s version of “Come from the Heart” is the song’s most well-known recording.\n- Kathy Mattea’s discography includes Top 10 singles, and “Come from the Heart” was one of four songs that reached #1 on the Billboard Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart, along with “Goin’ Gone,” “Eighteen Wheels and a Dozen Roses,” and “Burnin’ Old Memories.”",
        "type": "TextSummary"
